\newlabel{fig:cond-vs-uncond}{{1.4}{21}{The unconditional volatility (dashed red) is a single long-run average: it tells you nothing about which regime you're in today. The conditional volatility (solid blue) varies over time, spiking during crises and falling during calm periods. Your project's goal is to forecast the blue line one step ahead, not just know the red line}{figure.1.4}{}}
