\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.7}{\ignorespaces Decision tree for choosing a noise-robust estimator. For daily volatility forecasting, 5-min RV is the starting point. For intraday analysis or when estimation accuracy matters, use the realized kernel (default) or pre-averaging. TSRV is the simplest noise-robust estimator and a good starting point for learning.}}{50}{figure.3.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:estimator-flowchart}{{3.7}{50}{Decision tree for choosing a noise-robust estimator. For daily volatility forecasting, 5-min RV is the starting point. For intraday analysis or when estimation accuracy matters, use the realized kernel (default) or pre-averaging. TSRV is the simplest noise-robust estimator and a good starting point for learning}{figure.3.7}{}}
