\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.4}{\ignorespaces The decomposition pipeline. $\operatorname  {RV}_t$ is split into a continuous component $C_t$ (estimated via BPV or threshold truncation) and a jump component $J_t^2$ (the residual). The continuous component is highly persistent and drives forecasting accuracy. The jump component is nearly unpredictable but still included to prevent it from contaminating the continuous signal. In the HAR-J and HAR-CJ models, each component receives its own coefficient, letting the model exploit the different persistence.}}{65}{figure.4.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:decomposition-pipeline}{{4.4}{65}{The decomposition pipeline. $\RV _t$ is split into a continuous component $C_t$ (estimated via BPV or threshold truncation) and a jump component $J_t^2$ (the residual). The continuous component is highly persistent and drives forecasting accuracy. The jump component is nearly unpredictable but still included to prevent it from contaminating the continuous signal. In the HAR-J and HAR-CJ models, each component receives its own coefficient, letting the model exploit the different persistence}{figure.4.4}{}}
